1
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:54,000
In the Fire is a thriller, drama, horror film directed by Conor Allyn.

2
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:42,000
A doctor from New York travels to a remote plantation in the 1890s to care
for a disturbed boy who seems to have inexplicable abilities.

3
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:30,000
She begins treating the child, but in doing so, ignites a war between science and religion as the local
priest believes the boy is possessed by the devil and the cause of the village's woes.

4
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Grace Burnham, played by Amber Heard.

5
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Nicolas Marquez, played by Eduardo Noriega.

6
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Martin Marquez, played by Lorenzo McGovern Zaini.

7
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:42,000
Antonio, played by Luca Calvani.

8
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:30,000
Temo, played by Herbert Ignacio.

9
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:18,000
Maria, played by Monica Contini.

10
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
In the Fire is a 2023 thriller film directed by Conor Allyn, from a
screenplay by Allyn, Pascal Borno and Silvio Muraglia.

11
01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:54,000
It stars Amber Heard, Eduardo Noriega and Lorenzo McGovern Zaini.

12
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
It had its world premiere at the Taormina Film Festival on June 24, 2023, and was
released in the United States on October 13, 2023, by Saban Films.

13
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:30,000
The film explores themes of village, supernatural,
possession, priest, demonic possession.

14
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:18,000
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
